</script><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Food Crisis by Country: Latest Official Data and Updates | World Food Crisis</title><meta name="description" content="Country briefings on food prices and acute food insecurity, using dated official data from FAO, WFP, IPC, WHO and national statistics agencies."><link rel="canonical" href="https://worldfoodcrisis.pages.dev/food-crisis-by-country/"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"><script is:inline src="/assets/main.js" defer></script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"CollectionPage","name":"Food Crisis by Country: Latest Official Data and Updates","description":"Country briefings on food prices and acute food insecurity, using dated official data from FAO, WFP, IPC, WHO and national statistics agencies.","url":"https://worldfoodcrisis.pages.dev/food-crisis-by-country/","dateModified":"2026-10-15","inLanguage":"en","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"World Food Crisis","url":"https://worldfoodcrisis.pages.dev/"}}</script></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div class="topline"><div class="container topline-inner"><span>Independent food-system explainers</span><span>Facts before fear.</span></div></div><header class="site-header"><div class="container header-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">F<span>+</span></span><span class="brand-words"><strong>World Food Crisis</strong><small>Facts before fear.</small></span></a><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="primary-nav"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="sr-only">Open navigation</span></button><nav class="primary-nav" id="primary-nav"><a href="/#analysis">Analysis</a><a href="/data/">Data desk</a><a href="/#guides">Practical guides</a><a href="/about/">About</a></nav></div></header><main id="main"><header class="page-hero"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><span>Food crisis by country</span></nav><p class="section-kicker">Country data · Sources first</p><h1>Food Crisis by Country: Latest Official Data and Updates</h1><p>Country briefings that separate food-price inflation, local availability and acute food insecurity—and show the date, geography and limits of each official assessment.</p><p><strong>Last editorial check: 15 October 2026.</strong> Every number below belongs to a stated release and period; check the linked source for newer data before treating a forecast as current.</p></div></header><div class="container page-content"><div class="country-hub-intro"><h2>Start with the question you want answered</h2><p>A food-price index, an IPC food-insecurity classification and an early-warning report measure different things. A high inflation rate does not automatically prove physical shortage; a national food balance does not show every household's access. The pages below state what each source measures so readers can interpret claims accurately.</p></div><div class="country-hub-grid">
